# UAE Civil Transactions Law (Federal Law No. 5 of 1985), Article 390

Source: Federal Law No. 5 of 1985 (UAE Civil Transactions Law),
Article 390 — agreed compensation ("liquidated damages"). Pinned URL
in `uae_civil_code_art_390_source.yaml`. In force; current.

ATTRIBUTION (per RULES-ATTRIBUTION.md): The Arabic-language original
is © UAE Ministry of Justice. The English working translation
reproduced below is the form in widest circulation in UAE / DIFC /
ADGM litigation practice (drawn from the standard practitioner
editions; cross-checked against the Fenwick Elliott commentary on UAE
LD doctrine). Where competing translations exist, the encoding's
predicate logic does not depend on the precise English wording — the
Arabic-language original at the UAE Ministry of Justice is the
authoritative source for the rule of decision.

## Article 390 — verbatim text

Reproduced verbatim from the standard English translation of the UAE
Civil Transactions Law (Federal Law No. 5 of 1985):

Article 390(1):
"The contracting parties may fix the amount of compensation in advance
by making a provision therefor in the contract or in a subsequent
agreement, subject to the provisions of the law."

Article 390(2):
"The court may, on the application of either party, vary such
agreement so as to make the compensation equal to the loss and any
agreement to the contrary shall be void."

## Two distinct compensation-capping mechanisms

DOCTRINAL NOTE: this module captures **two distinct mechanisms** that
interact in the same case:

1. **Contract-clause LD cap.** The parties' own LD clause may itself
   cap the compensation at a percentage of contract value (e.g.
   `min(daily-rate × days, 10% of adjusted contract price)`). This cap
   is contractual, not statutory. It engages whenever the contract
   says it does — no court finding required.

2. **Article 390(2) variation.** The court has a separate, statutory
   discretion to *vary* the agreed compensation (whether contractually
   capped or not) to make it equal to the loss actually sustained.
   This power requires a predicate finding by the court: ADGM CFI
   case-law treats *gross disproportion* between the agreed sum and
   actual loss as the threshold for variation.

Both mechanisms can apply to the same case. In *Projeco v Ideacrate*
(trace-04) the contract's 10% cap engaged automatically; the
defendant *also* asked the court to vary the cap further down under
390(2), but the court refused that variation application because the
defendant had not proved the actual loss was less than the capped
amount. This module models both layers explicitly so the test data
can record what the contract did and what the court was asked to do
separately.

## Encoding

```catala
declaration structure LDClaim:
  data uncapped_amount_aed content decimal
  data contract_value_aed content decimal
  ## The contract's own LD cap (typically 10% of contract value in
  ## ADGM CFI commercial-construction practice). cap_rate = 0 means
  ## "no contractual cap; the LD clause is uncapped".
  data contract_cap_rate content decimal
  data contract_caps_ld content boolean
  ## A 390(2) variation application by the obligor. Independent of
  ## the contract cap. If true, the court's predicate finding on
  ## gross disproportion controls whether the variation engages.
  data court_asked_to_vary_under_390_2 content boolean
  data court_finds_grossly_disproportionate content boolean

declaration structure LDAward:
  data contract_cap_aed content decimal
  data after_contract_cap_aed content decimal
  data awarded_aed content decimal
  data was_contract_capped content boolean
  data was_390_2_varied content boolean

declaration scope Article390Cap:
  input claim content LDClaim
  output award content LDAward

scope Article390Cap:
  definition award equals
    ## Layer 1 — contract-clause cap. The cap value is only meaningful
    ## when contract_caps_ld is true; otherwise it is reported as 0.00
    ## to avoid leaking an inapplicable arithmetic value to downstream
    ## consumers.
    let raw_cap equals
      claim.contract_value_aed * claim.contract_cap_rate
    in
    let contract_cap equals
      if claim.contract_caps_ld then raw_cap else 0.00
    in
    let after_contract_cap equals
      if claim.contract_caps_ld
         and claim.uncapped_amount_aed > raw_cap then
        raw_cap
      else
        claim.uncapped_amount_aed
    in
    let was_contract_capped equals
      claim.contract_caps_ld
      and (after_contract_cap < claim.uncapped_amount_aed)
    in
    ## Layer 2 — Article 390(2) variation. The variation engages only
    ## where the court was asked AND made the gross-disproportion
    ## finding. The encoding does not compute the post-variation sum;
    ## the variation amount itself is a human-judgment input. The
    ## module records *whether* the variation engaged.
    let was_varied equals
      claim.court_asked_to_vary_under_390_2
      and claim.court_finds_grossly_disproportionate
    in
    ## In the typical case the variation does not further reduce the
    ## sum (because the court did not make the gross-disproportion
    ## finding). The awarded sum is the post-contract-cap sum.
    LDAward {
      -- contract_cap_aed: contract_cap
      -- after_contract_cap_aed: after_contract_cap
      -- awarded_aed: after_contract_cap
      -- was_contract_capped: was_contract_capped
      -- was_390_2_varied: was_varied
    }
```

## Used in

trace-04 — ADGMCFI-2024-320 *Projeco v Ideacrate*. The contract LD
clause capped damages at 10% of the adjusted contract price (AED
608,521.19). The obligor (Projeco) also applied under 390(2) for the
court to vary the LD further down; the court refused because Projeco
had not proved actual loss was less than the cap. The encoding now
records both layers separately: `was_contract_capped: true`,
`was_390_2_varied: false`.

## Tests

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestArt390ContractCapOnly_Trace04:
  composite scope Article390Cap
  output award content LDAward

scope TestArt390ContractCapOnly_Trace04:
  definition award equals composite.award
  ## trace-04: AED 9.7M uncapped LD, 10% contract cap on AED
  ## 6,085,211.90 contract = AED 608,521.19 cap engages. The
  ## obligor's 390(2) application was refused because the court did
  ## not find gross disproportion (defendant did not prove actual
  ## loss < cap).
  definition composite.claim equals
    LDClaim {
      -- uncapped_amount_aed: 9700000.00
      -- contract_value_aed: 6085211.90
      -- contract_cap_rate: 0.10
      -- contract_caps_ld: true
      -- court_asked_to_vary_under_390_2: true
      -- court_finds_grossly_disproportionate: false
    }
  assertion award.contract_cap_aed = 608521.19
  assertion award.after_contract_cap_aed = 608521.19
  assertion award.awarded_aed = 608521.19
  assertion award.was_contract_capped = true
  assertion award.was_390_2_varied = false

#[test] declaration scope TestArt390NoCapNoVariation:
  composite scope Article390Cap
  output award content LDAward

scope TestArt390NoCapNoVariation:
  definition award equals composite.award
  ## No contract cap, no 390(2) application — the agreed sum stands.
  definition composite.claim equals
    LDClaim {
      -- uncapped_amount_aed: 50000.00
      -- contract_value_aed: 1000000.00
      -- contract_cap_rate: 0.10
      -- contract_caps_ld: false
      -- court_asked_to_vary_under_390_2: false
      -- court_finds_grossly_disproportionate: false
    }
  assertion award.awarded_aed = 50000.00
  assertion award.was_contract_capped = false
  assertion award.was_390_2_varied = false

#[test] declaration scope TestArt390BothLayersEngage:
  composite scope Article390Cap
  output award content LDAward

scope TestArt390BothLayersEngage:
  definition award equals composite.award
  ## Hypothetical: contract caps at 10%, court ALSO finds gross
  ## disproportion under 390(2). The encoding records both layers as
  ## engaged; the post-variation sum is a human-judgment input not
  ## modelled here.
  definition composite.claim equals
    LDClaim {
      -- uncapped_amount_aed: 9700000.00
      -- contract_value_aed: 6085211.90
      -- contract_cap_rate: 0.10
      -- contract_caps_ld: true
      -- court_asked_to_vary_under_390_2: true
      -- court_finds_grossly_disproportionate: true
    }
  assertion award.was_contract_capped = true
  assertion award.was_390_2_varied = true
```
